Phase: Project Import/Export Full Fidelity Feature & Download Fix
Status: Verified & Completed
Date: 2026-10-29
App: Content Strategy Hub
Author: vlad@bluebeeweb.com

Summary of Changes:
- schemas.py:
  * Added ExportProjectParams, ExportProjectResult
  * Added ImportProjectParams, ImportProjectResult
- main.py:
  * Backend action export_project: extracts site_profile and all 14 related store collections:
    - opportunities
    - article_briefs
    - queue_items
    - site_competitors
    - content_audits
    - cannibalization_findings
    - existing_content_items
    - content_authors
    - content_decay_readings
    - content_decay_reports
    - kpi_snapshots
    - kpi_dashboards
    - outreach_targets
    - ile_status_cache
  * Backend action import_project: restores project and all collections with direct overwrite or ID remapping
  * UI in _project_tabs_view & brief_panel:
    - Fixed brief_panel to accept show_export and show_import parameters and forward them to _project_tabs_view. Previously, clicking Export or Import did nothing because brief_panel swallowed those parameters.
    - Added direct file download link (ui.Link with data:application/json base64 URI) in the Export dialog so clicking it downloads the .json file directly.
    - Added raw JSON textarea with Copy instructions.
- tests/test_smoke.py:
  * Comprehensive roundtrip test test_export_and_import_project_roundtrip verifying complete export/import fidelity across all collections.
- backup/:
  * Created pre-modification backups of main.py, schemas.py, and imperal.json.
